-- title:
--   Finiteness of Čech H⁰ for chart-finite two-chart data
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and let $\mathcal U$ be a two-chart cover datum over $R$, that is, three commutative $R$-algebras $A_0$, $A_1$, $A_{01}$ together with $R$-algebra maps $\rho_0 : A_0 \to A_{01}$ and $\rho_1 : A_1 \to A_{01}$. Let $S$ be a sections datum over $\mathcal U$: modules $M_0$ over $A_0$, $M_1$ over $A_1$ and $M_{01}$ over $A_{01}$, each also an $R$-module compatibly with the algebra action, together with $R$-linear maps $r_0 : M_0 \to M_{01}$ and $r_1 : M_1 \to M_{01}$ satisfying $r_0(a\,m) = \rho_0(a)\,r_0(m)$ for $a \in A_0$ and $r_1(a\,m) = \rho_1(a)\,r_1(m)$ for $a \in A_1$. Assume given $f \in A_0$ and $g \in A_1$ with $\rho_0(f)\,\rho_1(g) = 1$ in $A_{01}$, and the following four conditions: $M_0$ is a finite module over the $R$-subalgebra of $A_0$ generated by $f$ and $M_1$ is a finite module over the $R$-subalgebra of $A_1$ generated by $g$; every $m \in M_{01}$ satisfies $\rho_0(f)^n\,m \in r_0(M_0)$ for some $n \in \mathbb N$ and $\rho_1(g)^{n'}\,m \in r_1(M_1)$ for some $n' \in \mathbb N$; every $x \in M_0$ with $r_0(x) = 0$ is killed by some power of $f$; and every $y \in M_1$ with $r_1(y) = 0$ is killed by some power of $g$. Then the module `S.H0`, the zeroth Čech cohomology of the datum $S$, is a finite $R$-module.
--
--   This is the $H^0$ half of an elementary module-theoretic form of the finiteness of coherent cohomology of a proper curve over a Noetherian base (Serre's theorem for $\mathbb P^1$), the hypotheses encoding a coherent sheaf pushed forward along a finite map to $\mathbb P^1_R$ described chart-wise by $f$ and $g = 1/f$. Together with its companion [`TwoChartCech.Sections.finite_H1_of_chartFinite`](thm.html#TwoChartCech.Sections.finite_H1_of_chartFinite), which it cites along with [`TwoChartCech.kerMap_injective_of_H0_eq_zero`](thm.html#TwoChartCech.kerMap_injective_of_H0_eq_zero), it supplies the finiteness of $H^0$ and $H^1$ for line bundles and for sections data on a smooth proper curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_TwoChartCech_Sections_finite_H0_of_chartFinite.lean

import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicGeometry_TwoChartCech
